{
  "step_1": "The decision reason is based on an aspiration level defined as the mean of all outcomes across both lotteries, ignoring probabilities. The outcomes in the decision problem are 4000, 0 (from Lottery B), and 3000 (from Lottery A). The mean of these outcomes is (4000 + 0 + 3000) / 3 = 2333.33 Euros. This is the aspiration level. Next, the differences between each outcome and this aspiration level are computed: for Lottery A, 3000 - 2333.33 = +666.67 (positive difference); for Lottery B, 4000 - 2333.33 = +1666.67 (positive), and 0 - 2333.33 = -2333.33 (negative). The reason then evaluates the probability of achieving a positive difference: Lottery A has 100% probability (its only outcome is above aspiration), while Lottery B has 80% probability (4000 is above aspiration, 0 is below). Since 100% > 80%, the aspiration-level reason would prefer Lottery A. Thus, the reason is applicable and leads to a preference for A.",
