  "step_3": "The decision reason requires computing an aspiration level as the mean of all outcomes (1668.33) and comparing each outcome to this level to assess the probability of exceeding it. However, the individual only refers to the certainty of winning in A, showing a preference for guaranteed gains. The information considered by the individual (certainty of winning) is entirely different from the information required by the decision reason (deviations from an aspiration level). Furthermore, the justification (100% win) does not align with the rule of the decision reason, which would favor Lottery B due to its (small) chance of exceeding the high aspiration level. There is no evidence in the verbal report that the individual used or even considered such a calculation. Therefore, it is certain that the decision reason was not used.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
}

